  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "CONVERSION OF A SINGLE DWELLING HOUSE INTO 2 SELF CONTAINED UNITS",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide an additional dwelling, it would cause a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers, and would not be located in an area with a high level of access to public transport. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)-&nbsp;Policies&nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development would result in the addition of one household resulting in a maximum of 8 persons living within one terrace dwelling. Increasing the noise, disturbances and coming and goings. As such, the proposed development would significantly impact neighbouring dwellings and would be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals do not negatively impact existing neighbouring dwellings:- National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)-&nbsp;Policies D4, and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies SP2, and DMD1of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)",
    "The submission fails to demonstrate that the proposal would not result in a harmful impact and increased stress on&nbsp;parking within the surrounding streets. The proposal fails to provide adequate details regarding the allocation and management of parking. As such, the proposal is contrary to the following policies:- Policies T6 and&nbsp;T6.1 of the&nbsp;London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies SP8, and DMT 2 of&nbsp;&nbsp;the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037&nbsp;(September 2024)"
  ],
